README="# Exact-five Goal runtime CPU candidate\n\nThis is a new explicit-context package for Goal256 seed23/41 and Goal64 seed17/23/41, each one fresh100-state A/B200 attempt. The previous exclusive Goal256seed17 package and all173 frozen sources remain unchanged. This author package is a source/CPU candidate; it does not authorize a GPU, accept scientific results, reopen old Goal200, identify its cause, or open final/O2A.\n\nThe package manifest covers exactly20 production files:10 shared files and five independent config/specification pairs. Extra pre-version files are retained only as author provenance and must not be installed as production sources. The original CPU raw fixtures are preserved privately and wholly archived with member SHA/bytes; no synthetic blob is a production observation.\n\n## Fixed identity and original execution\n\nThe five plans come from the original scientific planner and their own original training provenance, with no borrowed source bridge. Config binds each exact scientific/effective/contract/execution-manifest/provenance/specification ref. The genuine prepared invocation is created only after real root and independent plan reviews; its template must exactly extend the effective plan. Root authorization subsequently pins its exact SHA. Training seed is23/41/17 as named; runtime seed17, environment seed0, wait10, chunk8, horizon300 remain fixed.\n\nA fresh plan has no historical output directory. Identity reconstruction reads the original development input panel named by original arguments, never creates a fake historical runroot. The prospective actual original_run is an explicit derived output. The adapter and scientific loop are reconstructed from pinned original sources. Original actions, success/failure, task/method order, reset/wait sequence, RNG and scientific model settings are retained.\n\nThe observer copies raw bytes and checks identity/dtype/shape/content before and after every query, and compares the five components plus instruction at all100 preB first queries. Passive simulator/RNG snapshots are checked without calling reset/step or changing inputs. Real calls are bounded by the original200 trials,60000 policy steps,7600 queries,2000 separate warmup steps and60s query watchdog. Ordinary unsuccessful task completion is retained. Input/storage/bound violations use BaseException fail-closed, so the legacy policy Exception branch cannot continue the next trial. A policy exception is retained in the original result before stopping this attempt.\n\nThe new trial AST adds pre-append exact-size guards to existing start/result/cleanup records. Each dictionary is evaluated once; serialized values and original append behavior are unchanged. Reverse AST projection verifies the original loop. A fresh privately loaded adapter has scoped append/publish prewrite size guards, restored in finally; original adapter source and run function are unchanged. No old exclusive package global is changed.\n\n## Explicit physical storage\n\nFor key K, X=results/formal_main_v2/execution/goal_remaining5_v1/K. P/X/attempt01 holds original_run and bounded outer metadata. R/results/formal_main_v2/raw_runtime/goal_remaining5_v1/K/attempt01 holds raw five-component blobs, passive simulator/RNG payloads, observer/events.jsonl, observer/gate.jsonl and runtime.stdout/runtime.stderr. No symlinks, deletion or data-reduction shortcut is used.\n\nAll five budgets are checked together on login and immediately before each own once-only claim. Same-filesystem needs are summed. No deduplication, expected release or claimed disk reservation is credited. Each P budget1137999872B; each R budget20945181504B. Five totals P5689999360B and R104725907520B. The exact root storage receipt is bound by config. Filesystem availability is not quota proof, can change afterward, and write failures stop while preserving prefix.\n\nP calculation:200*(4MiB result+64KiB cleanup+4096B start)+2*16MiB report(old+tmp)+16MiB config/panel+16MiB adapter original/copy+1024*64KiB outer+16MiB terminal+128MiB margin. The original summary report does not duplicate chunks; all potentially unbounded error/result text is guarded before its original append. Adapter append and publish are each bounded by4MiB/file; original pair and exact copy fit16MiB.\n\nR calculation:21032*(393288B observations+65536B RNG+8192B simulator+16384B capture record)+68032*16384B gate records+8GiB logs+1GiB margin. This is conservative against the exact original fixed-loop capture/gate counts. Every raw component/capture class retains its explicit byte guard; records are never truncated.\n\nScheduler bootstrap logs use R/results/slurm and are separately retained. After authorization and exclusive raw claim, the Python process opens its own runtime.stdout/stderr with O_EXCL and redirects there; it does not co-open the Slurm daemon files. RLIMIT_FSIZE2GiB/file applies to that process and children, not the Slurm daemon.4GiB is reserved in the calculation for the two runtime logs and another4GiB as conservative bootstrap-log allowance; the latter is explicitly not a daemon hardcap. Loading starts only after claim and redirection.\n\n## Root integration interfaces\n\n1. Validate the author delivery manifest and the20-file package_manifest, then obtain a different-agent source/CPU audit. Install only its exact production map and package_manifest to R/P canonical paths. Do not install private backups or CPU fixture code.\n2. Publish the five root/independent scientific plan reviews and run the plan author's exact prepare_after_reviews_v2 interface. Publish the genuine original invocations and all pinned metadata. Do not fabricate a historical output panel.\n3. Import entry and use context(key). Fresh metadata verification is verify_published(key,manifest_sha,must_be_fresh=True), or CLI --pair-key KEY --verify --package-manifest-sha256 SHA. It verifies all source/plan/input/checkpoint identities and whole-five storage, not GPU authorization.\n4. For each pair build genuine root and independent source readiness according to check_review(ctx,value,role,manifest_sha,config_sha), then root authorization according to validate_authorization(ctx,value,config_sha,manifest_sha,entry_sha). Each review must bind this full package map and own config. The separate exact-five dispatcher remains responsible for shared writerlock/CAS, all-modes eight-slot accounting, pair exclusivity, held submit, one ACK, pending reconciliation and one release. Runtime does not submit.\n5. Runtime validates exact reservation/held dispatch with validate_dispatch(ctx,dispatch,reservation,authorization,auth_sha,job_id,reservation_sha). Scheduler env variables are CTI_GOAL_REMAINING5_PAIR_KEY and CTI_GOAL_REMAINING5_AUTH_SHA256. No restart/automatic retry is permitted.\n6. Existing ACK reconciliation uses verify_existing_metadata(key,manifest_sha). It rebuilds exact source, original prepared input and identity; it neither claims a new directory nor repeats a new free-capacity admission. It returns status passed_existing_ACK_metadata_source_only and new_GPU_submission_allowed=false. This result cannot authorize a second submission.\n7. At a real terminal, exact-pull P/X/attempt01 metadata to R, retaining scheduler and original adapter originals/copies and all attempts/cost. Create a typed envelope with kind goal_remaining5_typed_terminal_manifest, execution_version goal-remaining5-prospective-single-attempt-v1, status complete_nonweight_pull, pair_key, package_manifest_sha256, authorization/dispatch/reservation refs, registered job and artifacts(path,sha256,bytes) below X/attempt01. Include raw_artifacts as complete actual absolute R rawroot inventory. Set weights_copied=false,sealed_values_read=false. consumer.review_terminal(R,ref) reconstructs original runtime/adapter/trajectory/rollout plus the complete raw gate. Save exact output, then consumer.consume(R,saved_ref) must reproduce it byte-for-value. This author has not run a new real-GPU terminal.\n8. Independent terminal review and root acceptance remain required. Retain failed attempts, allocation seconds and all negative results; no retry is implied by an error. Original Goal200 stays HOLD.\n\nCPU reports distinguish synthetic environments/policies from real read-only source/panel/capacity evidence. Five complete CPU panels each pass86 assertions; interface suite721/696 rejections, outer32/7, raw consumer146/135 and final bounded corrections36/8. The final consumer raw reconstruction AST is unchanged from its146-check version apart from scope pre-import SHA. Final scope pin, ACK-only capacity and exact written-byte corrections have dedicated tests.\n\nverify_saved.py --manifest-sha256 SHA validates every delivery file and every archive member without writing. Optional --replay-to must be a fresh direct R/.local/goal_remaining5_replay_* child; it copies exact private test/package bytes and executes only synthetic CPU suites there. All outputs and failures remain in that private child. Use the audited transport with exact entry SHA; never rerun finalizers over a frozen package.\n"
from pathlib import Path
import ast,gzip,hashlib,importlib.util,json,tarfile
D=Path('/share/home/u15016/XXY_CVPR/CTI-VLA/control_repo/.local/goal_remaining5_runtime_20261021T0449');Q=D/'package'
PKG='scripts/ops/formal_goal_remaining5_gate_v1'
def sha(p):
 h=hashlib.sha256()
 with Path(p).open('rb') as f:
  for b in iter(lambda:f.read(8<<20),b''):h.update(b)
 return h.hexdigest()
def record(p):return {'path':p.relative_to(D).as_posix(),'sha256':sha(p),'bytes':p.stat().st_size}
def write(p,obj):
 b=(json.dumps(obj,sort_keys=True,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2,allow_nan=False)+'\n').encode()
 with p.open('xb') as f:f.write(b)
 return record(p)
package=json.loads((Q/'package_manifest.json').read_bytes())
assert sha(Q/'package_manifest.json')=='200dcef220601fd26565bb48106856612853739f486f8374ef91a4967e60692f'
for rel,pin in package['files'].items():
 p=Q/Path(rel).relative_to(PKG);assert sha(p)==pin
 if p.suffix=='.py':ast.parse(p.read_text())
(D/'archives').mkdir();(D/'cpu_reports').mkdir()
archives=[];reports=[];total=0;counted_rejections=0
for source in sorted(D.glob('CPU_*')):
 if not source.is_dir():continue
 result=json.loads((source/'report.json').read_bytes())
 assert result['status'].startswith('passed') and all(r['passed'] for r in result['checks'])
 assert result['check_count']==len(result['checks'])
 total+=len(result['checks']);counted_rejections+=result.get('rejections',0)
 reportpath=D/'cpu_reports'/(source.name+'.json')
 with reportpath.open('xb') as f:f.write((source/'report.json').read_bytes())
 reports.append(dict(record(reportpath),check_count=len(result['checks']),rejections=result.get('rejections'),status=result['status']))
 members=[]
 paths=sorted(x for x in source.rglob('*') if x.is_file())
 for p in paths:
  assert not p.is_symlink()
  members.append({'path':p.relative_to(source).as_posix(),'sha256':sha(p),'bytes':p.stat().st_size})
 memberpath=D/'archives'/(source.name+'.members.json')
 write(memberpath,{'schema':'formal_main_v2','kind':'CPU_original_archive_members','source_root':str(source),'file_count':len(members),'files':members,'synthetic_not_scientific':True})
 archive=D/'archives'/(source.name+'.tar.gz')
 with archive.open('xb') as sink:
  with gzip.GzipFile(fileobj=sink,mode='wb',filename='',mtime=0,compresslevel=6) as gz:
   with tarfile.open(fileobj=gz,mode='w|',format=tarfile.PAX_FORMAT) as tf:
    for p,row in zip(paths,members):
     info=tarfile.TarInfo(row['path']);info.size=row['bytes'];info.uid=info.gid=0;info.uname=info.gname='';info.mode=0o644;info.mtime=0
     with p.open('rb') as f:tf.addfile(info,f)
 # Verify compressed membership and every original byte before freezing.
 with tarfile.open(archive,'r:gz') as tf:
  infos=tf.getmembers();assert len(infos)==len(members)
  for info,row in zip(infos,members):
   assert info.isfile() and info.name==row['path'] and info.size==row['bytes']
   stream=tf.extractfile(info);h=hashlib.sha256()
   for b in iter(lambda:stream.read(8<<20),b''):h.update(b)
   assert h.hexdigest()==row['sha256']
 archives.append({'archive_path':record(archive)['path'],'archive_sha256':sha(archive),'archive_bytes':archive.stat().st_size,'members_path':record(memberpath)['path'],'members_sha256':sha(memberpath),'file_count':len(members),'uncompressed_bytes':sum(v['bytes'] for v in members)})
 print(json.dumps({'archived':source.name,'files':len(members),'compressed_bytes':archive.stat().st_size}),flush=True)
assert total==1365 and counted_rejections==846
with (D/'README.md').open('x',encoding='utf8') as f:f.write(README)
r={'schema':'formal_main_v2','kind':'goal_remaining5_runtime_author_readiness','status':'passed_author_CPU_candidate_only_pending_independent_and_actual_P','reviewed_by':'author','package_manifest':record(Q/'package_manifest.json'),'package_manifest_sha256':sha(Q/'package_manifest.json'),'package_files':package['files'],'pair_keys':package['pair_keys'],'CPU_check_count':total,'explicit_rejections_in_nonloop_suites':counted_rejections,'checks_count_source':'immutable saved checks array lengths, no appended self-write check','reports':reports,'root_fixed_design':package['root_fixed_design'],'root_storage_decision':package['root_storage_decision'],'production_installed':False,'actual_P_verified':False,'actual_GPU_runtime_verified':False,'new_GPU_submissions':0,'new_scientific_results':0,'original200_HOLD':True,'final_release':False,'original_package_unchanged':True,'source173_verified_by_all_five_CPU_loops':True,'blockers':[],'production_blockers':['Different-agent final source/CPU audit and root source readiness required.','Actual published R/P closure, genuine prepared invocation, original wrapper/checkpoint identity and all-five capacity checks required.','Separate exact-five dispatcher shared-lock/CAS/held ACK/root single-attempt authorization required.','Each new real raw terminal must pass full original/typed consumer reconstruction, independent review and root acceptance.'],'preserved_pre_freeze_corrections':['Fresh original input panel replaces missing historical output panel dependency.','ACK-only metadata result has exact reconcile schema and does not re-admit capacity.','Outer/completion/parent guards bound exactly written encoding including indent/newline.','Entry and consumer pre-import pin scope source.','Parent gateway v2 missing pair keys was external and was not fixed by weakening this runtime.']}
write(D/'author_readiness.json',r)
files=[]
for p in sorted(D.rglob('*')):
 if not p.is_file():continue
 rel=p.relative_to(D)
 if rel.parts[0].startswith('CPU_'):continue
 assert not p.is_symlink() and p.name!='delivery_manifest.json'
 files.append(record(p))
manifest={'schema':'formal_main_v2','kind':'goal_remaining5_runtime_author_delivery','status':'frozen_CPU_candidate_not_production_admission','source_root':str(D),'file_count':len(files),'files':files,'CPU_archives':archives,'package_manifest_sha256':sha(Q/'package_manifest.json'),'production_file_count':20,'original_private_CPU_outputs_retained':True,'loose_synthetic_blobs_excluded_from_delivery_but_all_archived':True,'no_weights_or_sealed_values':True,'GPU_submissions':0,'production_writes':0,'original200_HOLD':True,'final_release':False}
ref=write(D/'delivery_manifest.json',manifest)
print(json.dumps({'delivery_manifest':ref,'author_readiness':record(D/'author_readiness.json'),'file_count':len(files),'CPU_check_count':total,'explicit_rejections':counted_rejections}),flush=True)
